===============================================================================
2. COLLECTED DATA — third-party terms apply
===============================================================================

The files under `data/` are not original work. They are collected from public
sources and remain subject to those sources' terms. The MIT licence above does
NOT cover them.

`data/cables.json`
    Submarine cable routes, landing points, owners and in-service dates.
    Source:  TeleGeography Submarine Cable Map
             https://www.submarinecablemap.com/
    Licence: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0
             https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/

    This is the reason this project is non-commercial. If you intend to use
    this repository commercially, remove `data/cables.json`, the `collect/
    cables.js` collector and the map's cable layer first — the rest of the
    project does not carry the NonCommercial restriction.

`data/global.json`, `data/members.json`, `data/networks.json`,
`data/peeringdb.json`
    Exchange, network and membership records.
    Source:  PeeringDB — https://www.peeringdb.com/
    Terms:   https://www.peeringdb.com/aup
    Attribution to PeeringDB is required. Records are self-reported by the
    networks themselves and are not verified.

`data/ports.json`, `data/traffic.csv`
    Port-level structure and aggregate traffic figures.
    Source:  bix.hu, operated by the Council of Hungarian Internet Providers
             (ISZT) — https://www.bix.hu/
    These are figures published openly by the operator. This project is not
    affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to ISZT or BIX.

`data/borders.json`
    Country boundary lines, simplified.
    Source:  Natural Earth — https://www.naturalearthdata.com/
    Licence: Public domain.

Map tiles displayed by the site are served by OpenStreetMap and are subject to
the ODbL: https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

